1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Welcome to the new feature introduction video of Marvelous Designer 2025.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
In this video, we will introduce you to the function of IK joint printing.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Since the start of the 2025 version, through the IK joint printing function, you can print the default Google IK joint point of Marvelous Designer on the FBX file imported from the outside.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
By printing the IK joint point, you can set up the posture and action files in the software for the virtual model.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Combining the automatic conversion of the new version with the action function, you can easily apply various actions for various virtual models to achieve different matching effects.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
First, I use the Mixamo web page to bind Google for virtual models, and then import it into Marvelous Designer.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Please modify the imported file to T-pose posture.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
When the file is confirmed,

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
please import it into Marvelous Designer.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
When you import the FBX file,

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
please note that the object type is selected as virtual model.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The default unit is mm.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Please note that you can select the unit that matches your own file.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Here you can cancel the auto-create arrangement point and the auto-create window.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Because the model we import is T-pose.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Then go to the virtual model option in the main menu,

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
click on the virtual model editor.

18
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
In the virtual model editor,

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
go to the IK joint option.

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Here you can adjust the IK joint setting of the virtual model,

21
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
or set up a set of IK joints for the virtual model.

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
You can choose to manually or automatically set up joints.

23
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
For manual setting,

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
you can click on the name of the IK joint,

25
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
then click on the Google joint corresponding to the virtual model,

26
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
and set up an IK joint for it.

27
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
For example, here,

28
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
click on the head,

29
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
then you will see the head joint in the test picture.

30
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
At this time, there is no corresponding IK joint,

31
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
so it is displayed as gray and white.

32
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Now select the head,

33
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
click on the virtual model head Google joint,

34
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
and complete the setting of the IK joint of the head.

35
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
You can repeat the steps until all the joints are set up.

36
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
After all the joints that must be set up are set up,

37
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
the state will be changed to normal.

38
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
In the default state,

39
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
the IK joint is symmetrical.

40
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
If you need an IK joint that is not symmetrical,

41
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
please click here to close the symmetry.

42
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
After completing the setting,

43
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
select the T-shape position,

44
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
then the reset position next to it will be activated.

45
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
So far, the IK joint setting has been completed.

46
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Next, let's see how to use automatic setting.

47
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Click on the automatic setting,

48
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
you will see the required IK joints have been set up.

49
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
As before, select the T-shape position,

50
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
then check if the reset position is automatically activated.

51
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
After the reset position button is activated,

52
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
the IK joint setting is complete.

53
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Then we can go to the asset library,

54
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
find the position file of the virtual model,

55
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
add a position,

56
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,000
you can see the virtual model that sets the IK joint,

57
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
so that the virtual model can be used once,

58
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
and you can also call the position or action file

59
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
in the shop.

60
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
After adding the IK joint,

61
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
the virtual model is ready to be used in the asset library.

62
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You can check whether the virtual model is set up

63
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
or not.

64
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
In the default state,

65
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
please click the IK joint setting function.

66
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Now you can choose the position

67
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
or action file.

68
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
This is how to add and konfirm IK joint.

